{% comment %}
The one shell every campaign renders through, whether its body came from a template or from
Markdown. Written once so the parts that must be right every time — the physical address and
the unsubscribe link — cannot be forgotten by whoever writes the body.

MJML compiles this to table-based HTML that survives Outlook's Word renderer. Do not
hand-edit the compiled output; edit here.

Two constraints this is built around:
  - Gmail clips messages over 102KB and hides the rest behind "View entire message" — which
    would hide the unsubscribe link. Keep bodies lean; reference images by URL, never inline.
  - Dark mode inverts unpredictably in Gmail and is ignored by Outlook, so every background
    and text colour is stated rather than left to a default.
{% endcomment %}<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title>{{ subject }}</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>{{ preheader }}</mj-preview>
    <mj-attributes>
      {% comment %}
        The system stack the previous Mailchimp campaigns used, so mail from us keeps looking
        like mail from us. Helvetica/Arial is the fallback for clients with no system font.

        Roboto is deliberately NOT in this list even though Mailchimp's stack had it: MJML
        recognises Google font names and helpfully adds a <link> to fonts.googleapis.com, which
        would make every email fetch a resource from Google on open. That is a tracking vector,
        it contradicts what the privacy page promises, and most clients strip it anyway.
      {% endcomment %}
      <mj-all font-family="-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" />
      {% comment %}
        Centred everywhere, set once here rather than per block — MJML's default is left, which
        is what left half the email ranged left and half centred.
      {% endcomment %}
      <mj-text font-size="16px" line-height="1.6" color="#222222" align="center" />
      <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  {% comment %}640px, the width the Mailchimp campaigns used.{% endcomment %}
  <mj-body background-color="#f4f4f4" width="640px">

    {% comment %}
      A masthead rather than a favicon: the logo carried the identity in the old campaigns and
      it is the first thing a reader recognises. Linked, because people click logos. The name in
      letterspaced caps only appears when there is no logo to carry it.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% comment %}
      Conditioned on the resolved URL, not on site.icon: an icon that exists but whose derived
      email-sized copy could not be produced must fall back to the wordmark, because a broken
      image cannot be fixed once the mail is sent.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if site_icon_url %}
    <mj-section padding="24px 0 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="{{ site_icon_url }}" width="147px" alt="{{ site_name }}"
                  href="{{ site_url }}" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    {% else %}
    <mj-section padding="24px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="13px" color="#888888" letter-spacing="1px">
          <a href="{{ site_url }}" style="color:#888888;text-decoration:none">{{ site_name|upper }}</a>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    {% endif %}

    {{ body_mjml }}

    {% comment %}
      "Come Visit" — hours, how to reach a human, and a link that opens the address in a map.
      Part of the shell rather than each campaign, which is the whole difference from writing
      these by hand: nobody retypes opening hours, and nobody sends the old ones.

      Every line is conditional. A venue that has not filled in its hours gets a shorter block,
      not an empty heading.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% comment %}
      Gated on the fields that carry something a visitor can use. Deliberately NOT on
      postal_address, which is never empty — the country defaults in, so a venue that has filled
      in nothing at all still has an address of "United States of America", and the heading
      rendered above nothing.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if site.hours_display or site.visit_notes or site.phone or site.email or site.street %}
    <mj-section padding="16px 24px 0" background-color="#f7f7f7">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" padding="12px 0 6px">Come visit the gallery</mj-text>
        {% if site.hours_display %}<mj-text padding="0 0 6px">{{ site.hours_display }}</mj-text>{% endif %}
        {% if site.visit_notes %}<mj-text padding="0 0 6px">{{ site.visit_notes|striptags|truncatewords:40 }}</mj-text>{% endif %}
        {% if site.phone or site.email %}
        <mj-text padding="0 0 6px">
          To arrange a time:
          {% if site.phone %}<a href="tel:{{ site.phone }}" style="color:#198754">{{ site.phone }}</a>{% endif %}
          {% if site.phone and site.email %} or {% endif %}
          {% if site.email %}<a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Gallery%20visit" style="color:#198754">{{ site.email }}</a>{% endif %}
        </mj-text>
        {% endif %}
        {% comment %}
          Street and city only, not the full postal address: the footer below carries that in
          full because CAN-SPAM requires it, and printing it twice reads like a mistake. What is
          useful here is the link, not the country line.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% if site.street %}
        <mj-text padding="0 0 14px">
          {% if maps_url %}<a href="{{ maps_url }}" style="color:#198754">{{ site.street }}{% if site.city %}, {{ site.city }}{% endif %} — directions</a>{% else %}{{ site.street }}{% if site.city %}, {{ site.city }}{% endif %}{% endif %}
        </mj-text>
        {% endif %}
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if site.instagram or site.website %}
    <mj-section padding="12px 24px 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="14px">
          {% if site.instagram %}<a href="https://www.instagram.com/{{ site.instagram|cut:"@" }}/" style="color:#198754">Instagram</a>{% endif %}
          {% if site.instagram and site.website %}&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;{% endif %}
          {% if site.website %}<a href="{{ site.website }}" style="color:#198754">{{ site_name }}</a>{% endif %}
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    {% endif %}

    <mj-section padding="8px 0 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-color="#e0e0e0" padding="16px 0" />
        {% comment %}
          CAN-SPAM requires a physical postal address in every marketing email. It comes from
          the venue's own record, so a network of galleries each carries the right one
          without anybody remembering to change it.
        {% endcomment %}
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" color="#888888" line-height="1.6">
          {{ site_name }}{% if postal_address %}<br />{{ postal_address }}{% endif %}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" color="#888888">
          You are receiving this because you opted in at {{ site_name }}.<br />
          <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:#888888">Unsubscribe</a>
          &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
          <a href="{{ privacy_url }}" style="color:#888888">Privacy</a>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
